[{"id":50979,"sender_id":285,"sender_full_name":"Fosco","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/80b4e8d901cc7a9df4a4c539c5d33000?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/hearts.20and.20towers.20in.20stable.20.24.5Cinfty.24-categories/near/50979\">#1</a> Domenico Fiorenza and I are completing a <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/eqbwis0qwbg9rxv/a-brand-new-file.pdf\">paper</a> about hearts of t-structures in stable <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-categories, which shows that in the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-categorical setting semiorthogonal decompositions on a stable <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-category <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0583em;\">C</span></span></span></span> arise decomposing morphisms in the <em>Postnikov tower</em> induced by a chain of t-structures, regarded (thanks to our previous <a href=\"http://arxiv.org/abs/1408.7003\">work</a>) as multiple factorization systems on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0583em;\">C</span></span></span></span>. </p>\n<p>A slightly unexpected result is that t-structures having stable classes, i.e. those <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">C</mi><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"script\">C</mi><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\mathcal{C}_{\\ge 0}, \\mathcal{C}_{\\lt 0})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0583em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0583em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mrel mtight\">≥</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2452em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0583em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0583em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mrel mtight\">&lt;</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1774em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> such that both classes are stable <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-subcategories of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathcal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0583em;\">C</span></span></span></span>, are precisely the <em>fixed points</em> for the natural action of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span></span></span></span> on the set of t-structures, given by the shift endofunctor.</p>\n<p>As always, any comment, suggestion, criticism is welcome.</p>","timestamp":1421082152,"subject":"hearts and towers in stable $\\infty$-categories","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":50988,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/hearts.20and.20towers.20in.20stable.20.24.5Cinfty.24-categories/near/50988\">#2</a> Speaking of t-structures, apparently there is a closely related notion of a <em>weight structure</em>\non a triangulated category (see the papers by Bondarko),\nwhich axiomatizes chain complexes equivalent to those concentrated in nonnegative resp. nonpositive degrees,\nas opposed to t-structures, which axiomatize chain complexes whose homology is concentrated\nin nonnegative resp. nonpositive degrees.</p>\n<p>Are you aware of any treatments of weight structures in the context of stable ∞-categories?</p>","timestamp":1421193714,"subject":"hearts and towers in stable $\\infty$-categories","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":50990,"sender_id":285,"sender_full_name":"Fosco","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/80b4e8d901cc7a9df4a4c539c5d33000?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/hearts.20and.20towers.20in.20stable.20.24.5Cinfty.24-categories/near/50990\">#3</a> Can you provide us a pointer with the definition of weight structure? There are several papers in <a href=\"http://arxiv.org/find/math/1/au:+Bondarko_M/0/1/0/all/0/1\">Bondarko’s arxiv list</a> (NP, just found <a href=\"http://arxiv.org/pdf/0704.4003.pdf\">this</a>.. but any other reference is welcome!)</p>","timestamp":1421237219,"subject":"hearts and towers in stable $\\infty$-categories","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":50994,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/hearts.20and.20towers.20in.20stable.20.24.5Cinfty.24-categories/near/50994\">#4</a> @Fosco: Yes, 0704.4003 is the right reference.</p>","timestamp":1421246156,"subject":"hearts and towers in stable $\\infty$-categories","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":51105,"sender_id":39,"sender_full_name":"domenico_fiorenza","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8a7724cd61dd2245b88f48716b64b4d5?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/hearts.20and.20towers.20in.20stable.20.24.5Cinfty.24-categories/near/51105\">#5</a> We have now uploaded on arXiv. The comparison with eight structures suggested by Dmitri is indeed very interesting but we realized it needed a development going beyond the aims of the present paper, so we postponed it to a (hopefully) forthcoming follow-up.</p>","timestamp":1421710123,"subject":"hearts and towers in stable $\\infty$-categories","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":51130,"sender_id":147,"sender_full_name":"Dmitri Pavlov","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7c66d1b7cad17c58076e0f3d13220d63?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/hearts.20and.20towers.20in.20stable.20.24.5Cinfty.24-categories/near/51130\">#6</a> @domenico_fiorenza: I would be very interested in reading such a followup.</p>","timestamp":1421850698,"subject":"hearts and towers in stable $\\infty$-categories","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]}]